@*
    The running build's version, for us rather than for the operator.

    Two callers today — the settings page, for when you are signed in, and the sign-in screen, for
    when you cannot get that far. The null check and the development marker live here rather than in
    both of them, because the marker is the part that must not be forgotten: 1.0.0 is what a local
    build reports and also what an untagged web deployment reports, so a bare number would read as a
    release either way. See AppVersion.
*@
@if (AppVersion.Display is { } version)
{
    <span class="@Class">
        @(AppVersion.IsDevelopmentBuild
            ? L["App.VersionDevelopment", version]
            : L["App.Version", version])
    </span>
}

@code {
    [Parameter] public string? Class { get; set; }
}
